                    <div class="moiss-val-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-seedling"></i></div>
                    <h3 class="moiss-val-title">Sustainable & Conflict-Free</h3>
                    <p class="moiss-val-desc">In addition to offering a size chart for reference, we take immense pride in stating that our lab-grown diamonds and moissanite are ethical, sustainable, and conflict-free, cultivated without soil erosion or carbon-heavy mining footprints.</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Card 4 -->
                <div class="moiss-val-card">
                    <div class="moiss-val-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i></div>
                    <h3 class="moiss-val-title">Uncompromising Durability & Hardness</h3>
                    <p class="moiss-val-desc">Both lab-grown diamonds (10/10 Mohs scale) and moissanite (9.25–9.50 Mohs scale) are exceptionally resilient gemstones crafted for daily elegance and lifetime wear, offering supreme scratch resistance against daily wear.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Have Any Questions FAQ Accordion (From media_1787461024024.md) -->
    <div style="max-width: 1000px; margin: 60px auto 40px; padding: 0 24px;">
        <h2 style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: 700; text-align: center; color: #ffffff; margin-bottom: 32px;">Have Any Questions?</h2>

        <div style="background: #0b1524; color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px; box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(212, 178, 112, 0.25);">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0 0 10px;">Why do Moissanite and Lab-Grown Diamonds differ in weight for the same dimensions?</h3>
            <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
                Moissanite and diamonds have distinct physical densities. Moissanite is composed of silicon carbide, making it approximately 10–12% lighter in density than a carbon-based diamond. Consequently, two stones with the exact same millimeter dimensions will vary in carat weight. To maintain clarity for our customers, Sat Jewels lists moissanite sizes by both millimeter measurements and Diamond Equivalent Weight (DEW).
            </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: #0b1524; color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px; box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(212, 178, 112, 0.25);">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0 0 10px;">Does Moissanite display a strong rainbow fire effect?</h3>
            <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
                Because moissanite has a higher refractive index than diamond, it naturally disperses brilliant spectral colors. However, at Sat Jewels, our master gem cutters utilize specialized precision-cut techniques designed to minimize excess rainbow fire, giving our moissanite a refined, elegant, and diamond-like luster.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: #0b1524; color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px; box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(212, 178, 112, 0.25);">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0 0 10px;">Moissanite vs. Lab-Grown Diamond: Which should I choose?</h3>
            <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 10px;">
                Both offer exceptional beauty, so the ideal selection depends on your priorities:
            </p>
            <ul style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; padding-left: 20px; margin: 0;">
                <li><strong>Moissanite:</strong> Highly durable, budget-friendly, and offers maximum sparkle and brilliance.</li>
                <li><strong>Lab-Grown Diamonds:</strong> Chemically, physically, and optically identical to mined diamonds, offering timeless prestige, classic luster, and a 10/10 hardness rating.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div style="background: #0b1524; color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px; box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(212, 178, 112, 0.25);">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0 0 10px;">Are Lab-Grown Diamonds real diamonds?</h3>
            <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
                Yes, absolutely. Lab-grown diamonds possess the exact chemical composition, crystal structure, and optical properties as mined diamonds. The only distinction is their origin—they are cultivated in technologically advanced environments rather than extracted from the earth.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: #0b1524; color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px; box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(212, 178, 112, 0.25);">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0 0 10px;">Can I wear a Lab-Grown Diamond as my official birthstone?</h3>
            <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
                Definitely. Since lab-grown diamonds are authentic diamonds, they serve as a perfect April birthstone option. They provide identical optical elegance and physical strength while offering a completely ethical, sustainable choice.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

